      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T08:55:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just wondering why we are not using the github3py API for getting a branch?\nhttps://github3.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api-reference/repos.html#github3.repos.repo.Repository.branch\n\nI think in the past we only used the lower-level API when there was no support in gh3py yet or the client was making unnecessary requests.\n\nI\u0027m mainly asking as I think the error handling here is spotty in that we only handle 403 and 404 and in all other error cases line we\u0027ll probably get a JSON decode error or a key error (depending on the response format).",
      "revId": "a9dc6b03c2898c0dd2f9fb27fd78476cc3caa07a",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a886de5f_de3cde10",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/github/githubconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1845,
      "author": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-14T22:29:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We currently do this in 2 places, this adds a third.\n\nHere\u0027s a comment in one of the 2 existing ones that confirms it\u0027s about making unnecessary requests: https://opendev.org/zuul/zuul/src/branch/master/zuul/driver/github/githubconnection.py#L1848-L1852\n\nI feel like since error handling on this request is not more critical than our existing code, we don\u0027t need to put the onus of changing that on this change.  In other words, it should be good enough to do what we already do.\n\nAs for what we should do in general: if we think that any of the code paths still warrant the extra efficiency of avoiding creating a repo object, then we may as well make a really nice method for getting branches and put all the error handling we want in there, and then call it from all 3 locations.\n\nIf we don\u0027t think any code path needs that any more, then I\u0027d say let\u0027s change all 3 to use ghpy.\n\nRegardless, I think we can handle that in a later change.",
      "parentUuid": "1da049ed_73b1e89c",
      "revId": "a9dc6b03c2898c0dd2f9fb27fd78476cc3caa07a",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
